ps4-pkg-tool
============

The Rebuild Tool unpacks PS4 fake PKGs (the game and its update) with ps4-pkg-tool, a command line program run by the tool. It is a separate
executable (shipped next to bb-recomp), not linked into it.

Source:   https://github.com/xXJSONDeruloXx/ps4-pkg-tools (commit 45baedaa29b8da42b3c6fe912800d2fa4119834b)
License:  GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version
          (SPDX GPL-2.0-or-later). Copyright (C) 2024 shadPS4 Emulator Project and contributors;
          its PKG/PFS code is shadPS4's (https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4).
Changes:  this project applies the patches in shared/pkg-tool/patches/ (system zlib, byte progress,
          64-bit sizes and offsets for multi-GB PKGs, refusal of file names that leave the output
          folder) and builds it with shared/pkg-tool/build_pkg_tool.sh. The complete corresponding
          source is the upstream commit above plus those patches, both in this repository (the
          fetch script fetches the upstream commit). The GPL-2.0 license text is at
          https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt

